<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Demak Sultanate</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sultanate of Demak</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Demak Sultanate was the first major Muslim state on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>, based on the island's north coast. Its rise in the late fifteenth and early sixteenth centuries contributed to the final collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hindu-buddhist">Hindu-Buddhist</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit Empire</a> and to the spread of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> across Java.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/demak-sultanate.jpg" alt="Demak Sultanate" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mhatopzz · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MUS_Koin_Sultan_Pangeran_Raden_Fatah.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
